[profiles.guide]
notes = '''This is the gyro variant: tilting the controller moves the cursor, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}. Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
The right stick {rs} moves the cursor: {rt} selects (left click, hold to drag a box), and {lt} moves, gathers, builds or attacks (right click). The left stick {ls} scrolls the map, and {up} {down} zoom.
{south} jumps to the next idle villager, {west} to idle military and {north} to the Town Center. {left} opens the Home City to send a shipment, and {right} finds your Explorer.
Hold {lb} for the control groups and aim the right stick {rs} at one: release to select it. Hold {lb} and {rb} together to put the selection in a group instead (Ctrl + number).
{rb} is Shift: hold it to queue orders, add to the selection, or train five at once. Double-click with {rt} to select every unit of that type on screen.
Click {r3} for the unit commands (stop, ungarrison, delete), aimed with the right stick {rs}.
{select} lists pause, chat and the Home City. Hold {select} for the Menus mode (lobbies, the Home City screens, the main menu) and hold it again to come back. {start} (Esc) is the game menu; {east} cancels and closes.
The keys are the Definitive Edition's defaults, assumed to match the 2005 game's and not checked on an install: the Home City (C), Explorer (/), pause and the unit commands are the likeliest to differ. If a key does nothing, look in Options, Hotkeys. The base game, The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties run as age3.exe, age3x.exe and age3y.exe; age3x.exe isn't in the detection list and is from memory. Guide + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard for chat.'''

